# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Conventional Commits. A scope is required (house rule); never omit it.
# Allowed types:
#   feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, build, revert
# Scope: the module or area touched. For this repo:
#   plans, actuals, reports, auth, categories, locks, imports, audit, nl-query,
#   platform, scaffold, docker, seed.
# For cross-cutting work use: repo, deps, ci, config, docs.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(locks): reject edits to a locked month with 423
#   fix(reports): return null for variance percent when the plan is zero
#   docs(readme): document the missing actual policy
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period; header under 100 chars.
# Body (optional): leave a blank line, then explain what changed and why; wrap at 100.
# Footer (optional): BREAKING CHANGE: <description>, or Refs: <id>.
#
# commitlint enforces this format via the Husky commit-msg hook.
